
Open the asymmetric assembly path to user elements, and fix the signed char
node count.

U3 (patch 0002) has a non-symmetric matrix by construction: the F-bar pairing
takes the stress from the modified gradient and pairs it with the virtual work
of the unmodified one (K_vol = (K V_h) tbar^T sbar, tbar != sbar; the Galerkin
form sbar^T sbar is a different element).  ccx already carries a complete
asymmetric path for friction contact; three things kept U3 out of it.

1. nasym was raised too late.  An element raising it inside e_c3d_u is
   silently symmetrised by mafillsm and then double-counted by mafillsmas, so
   linstatic.c and nonlingeo.c scan for "U3" and set nasym before
   mafillsmmain, and mafillsm.f skips U3 when nasym is set.
2. The asymmetric mechanical loop covered contact only (range ne0+1..ne,
   empty without contact), so the whole volumetric half was missing from the
   matrix while neq and the sparsity looked right.  mafillsmasmain.c
   partitions 1..ne when a U3 is present; mafillsmas.f calls e_c3d_u3 into
   allocatable wide arrays, sized to 765 only when the thread's range holds a
   U3, so the fixed .bss does not grow.
3. mastruct.c, mastructcs.c and arpackcs.c read the node count from a signed
   char, so a >127-node element read negative and got no structure.  Fixed
   with an (unsigned char) cast.

VERIFIED: patch test and confined compression, c = 0, 1, 2, match the C3D4
control to the last printed digit; every U3 deck factors with the unsymmetric
PARDISO; global force balance |sum RF|/max|RF| <= 7.1e-15.


